@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam RoundCorner 8
skinparam ParticipantPadding 25
skinparam BoxPadding 15
skinparam maxMessageSize 235
skinparam DefaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam TitleFontSize 20
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #555555
    ArrowFontName SansSerif
    ArrowFontSize 11
    LifeLineBorderColor #BDC3C7
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #ECF0F1
    ParticipantBorderColor transparent
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #34495E
    ParticipantFontName SansSerif
    ParticipantFontSize 13
    ParticipantFontColor white
    BoxBorderColor transparent
    BoxFontName SansSerif
    BoxFontSize 11
    BoxFontColor #6F8592
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
    BorderColor #FBC02D
    FontName SansSerif
    FontSize 11
    FontColor #424242
}

title One operator, its watches, and the Karta SDK
actor "Kubernetes API" as API
box "Your operator process: caller-owned lifecycle" #EAF2F8
participant "Watch + queue\nRead current state" as Controller
participant "Karta SDK\nOwnership + interpretation" as SDK
participant "Definition registry\nSelected exact GVKs" as Definitions
database "Your output\nInventory / product / metrics" as Output
end box
legend left
  Blue: object observation and queued work
  Green: definition publication
  Gray: local result and consumer decision
endlegend
== A. Select and publish definitions ==
Controller -[#24936E]> Definitions: NewDefinitionRegistry(selected catalog entries)
Definitions --> Controller: validated immutable definitions
Controller -> SDK: NewDiscoverer(reader, DefinitionProvider)
SDK --> Controller: reusable SDK; no watches started
note over Controller,Definitions
  Caller owns client, cache scope, readiness and retries.
  A deliberately empty registry is valid generic mode.
  An unsynchronized external source must remain gated.
end note
== B. A Pod changes ==
API -[#367DC4]> Controller: Pod event -> enqueue namespace/name
Controller -[#367DC4]> API: worker reads current Pod
API --> Controller: Pod with current UID
Controller -> SDK: WorkloadForPod(ctx, PodReference(pod))
SDK -> Controller: reader.Mapping / Get
Controller --> SDK: verified root chain
note over Controller,SDK
  Direct-reader flow shown here. Index queries instead
  capture one complete generation before definition lookup.
  A scheduler-filtered list is not complete coverage.
end note
SDK -> Definitions: Definition(ctx, root GVK)
alt matching definition
  Definitions --> SDK: immutable compiled definition
  SDK -> Controller: reader.ListPods + verify owner closure
  Controller --> SDK: complete Pod coverage
  SDK --> Controller: workload + Pods + component memberships
else confirmed absence
  Definitions --> SDK: nil, nil
  SDK -> Controller: reader.ListPods + verify owner closure
  Controller --> SDK: complete Pod coverage
  SDK --> Controller: same workload + Pods; generic pods component
else provider unavailable
  Definitions --> SDK: error
  SDK --> Controller: error; no generic success
  Controller -> Controller: retain output; retry under caller policy
end
opt successful observation
  Controller -> Output: replace record for workload UID
end
== C. A Karta definition changes or is deleted ==
API -[#24936E]> Controller: Karta event -> enqueue definition reconciliation
Controller -> Controller: serialized worker reads current selected set
Controller -[#24936E]> Definitions: Replace(selected...)
alt valid complete selection
  Definitions --> Controller: atomically published; omitted entries removed
  Controller -> Controller: enqueue affected workload roots
  Controller -> SDK: Workload(ctx, rootRef)
  SDK -> Definitions: Definition(ctx, root GVK)
  Definitions --> SDK: current definition or confirmed absence
  SDK --> Controller: newly interpreted observation
  Controller -> Output: update existing record
else invalid selection
  Definitions --> Controller: error; previous selection remains
  Controller -> Controller: expose failure and retry
end
note over SDK,Definitions
  Previously returned observations keep their definition.
  Changing a definition does not change ownership roots.
end note
== D. A Pod disappears ==
API -[#367DC4]> Controller: delete or tombstone -> enqueue key
Controller -[#367DC4]> API: GET current Pod
API --> Controller: NotFound
Controller -> Output: read saved Pod-to-workload association
Output --> Controller: previous workload reference
Controller -> SDK: Workload(ctx, previousRoot)
SDK --> Controller: remaining Pods, or root-read error
Controller -> Output: refresh workload; remove only confirmed deleted records
note over Controller,SDK
  Never discover a deleted Pod by calling WorkloadForPod.
  Reparenting also refreshes the saved former workload.
end note
@enduml
